WEBVTT

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:02.350
Well, let's get crackin'.

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:03.580
Let's-a-go.

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:05.920
Stop messing around and start!

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:31.330
On this day...

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:33.250
...the sunniest day in autumn...

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:35.840
...athletic festivals are being held all over the country.

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:36.800
Man...

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:38.460
I came to cheer for my daughter...

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:40.220
...but I didn't expect such a turnout.

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:41.760
This was worth the trip.

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:44.760
I got some great pictures.

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:45.100
Look.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:45.180
Dad.

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:46.560
Isn't this a great shot?

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:46.640
If you put it like this...

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:48.560
Which daughter are you talking about?

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:55.440
Maybe I should cut my hair for the athletic festival.

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:56.820
Go for a really short look.

00:01:57.690 --> 00:01:59.440
You're going to cut your hair?

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:01.320
But it took forever to grow it so long.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:06.030
I wasn't that serious about it...

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:08.200
That profound response...

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:09.330
...must have something to do with a guy!

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:11.250
Stop connecting everything to that subject!

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:12.790
And you stop talking so much!

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.040
But if Kagami cut her hair...

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:17.000
<i>That's what I heard...</i>

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.550
<i>...but it's not unusual, right?</i>

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:19.420
Ya can't!

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:21.840
Bipolar girls hafta have twin pigtails!

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.050
Sorry I have a boring face!

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:25.090
Oh, yeah.

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:26.890
The athletic festival's coming up.

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:28.180
Sounds like a pain.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:30.560
Wouldn't expect to hear that from a young person.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:33.100
Kona-chan's good at sports so she's okay...

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:34.850
...but someone like me...

00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:36.190
...just drags everyone down.

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:37.400
Don't worry.

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:42.200
What event are you doing, Sis?

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.320
Well, it's Kagami, so you know...

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:45.740
A bread eating contest.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:47.660
I've been wondering...

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:49.580
Are you trying to pick a fight or something?

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:52.750
So what are you going to do, Kagami?

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.040
I guessed right?

00:02:58.040 --> 00:02:59.170
Did I guess right?

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:00.170
She pisses me off!

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:04.090
So I plan on doing some
independent training for the athletic festival.

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:05.510
Since fall is for sports.

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:10.140
But are you really training for the athletic festival?

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:13.020
Aren't you actually training
for the main event afterwards?

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:15.010
What do you mean?

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:20.360
You want me to say it?

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:21.940
<i>She really pisses me off!</i>

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:25.530
So Miyuki's participating in the inter-class relay.

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:26.820
Well, I can understand that one.

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:30.950
She was originally supposed
to be in the obstacle course.

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:31.990
Okay.

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:33.700
No more candidates, right?

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:36.710
I've never tried it so I can't wait.

00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:38.670
That's no good, Miyuki-san!

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:43.510
Your body sticks out too much for an obstacle course.

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:44.590
You'd have to go through stuff.

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:47.890
After I said that, she was switched to the relay.

00:03:47.890 --> 00:03:50.680
Isn't that something a middle-aged guy would say?

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:51.850
Oh, yeah.

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:55.350
Did you guys ever have a
scavenger race in middle school?

00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:56.730
Sure did.

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:59.480
I was called up once...

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:00.060
Me?

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:06.650
...but he never told me what the criteria were.

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:09.320
<i>Too many unspeakable things come to mind.</i>

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:12.700
Well, just ask Miyuki-san
when you don't know the answer.

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:14.080
Don't ask her something like that.

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:15.830
It's impossible to answer.

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:17.790
<i>And she really went and asked...</i>

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.830
A character trait that would
come up in a scavenger race...

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:22.670
...that people wouldn't want to tell you about?

00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:28.720
Perhaps he needed a person with a mole on her face.

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:31.100
Some people are sensitive about that.

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:32.640
<i>I guess it was expected...</i>

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:34.720
<i>...but that was one masterful dodge.</i>

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:36.310
<i>But I'm pretty sure she's wrong.</i>

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:41.400
I enjoy athletic festivals...

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:43.610
...but we have tests right after.

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:45.320
Once the festival's over...

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:48.610
...there aren't any more events which is kind of sad.

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:49.360
Midterms.

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:50.110
Practical exams.

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:50.950
Finals.

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:52.580
All we have are tests.

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:54.160
The second semester is a drain on your energy

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:57.540
with events like the cultural
festival and the athletic festival.

00:04:57.540 --> 00:04:58.250
Right?

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:00.880
Midterms are particularly rough.

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:04.710
They also say that fall is for reading...

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:06.460
...so maybe I should read something.

00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:09.590
It's also a good season to study for tests.

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:12.970
And there's a whirlwind of
new game releases before Christmas!

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:15.260
But finals come first.

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:19.270
Oh, yeah!

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:19.980
You two.

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:22.770
Could you stop trying to avoid reality?

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:27.490
I see.

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:29.360
The athletic festival's coming up, huh?

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:31.450
You know about the starter's pistol?

00:05:31.450 --> 00:05:34.490
I thought it was a real gun until middle school.

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:35.450
No way...

00:05:35.450 --> 00:05:39.290
That was when I knew I wanted to be a cop.

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:41.960
<i>That misunderstanding led
to something totally unrelated.</i>

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:44.500
That's right, Konata.

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:47.130
When's the athletic festival at your school?

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:48.940
This Sunday.

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:52.300
Th-This Sunday?!

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:54.890
Why didn't you tell me
such an important thing earlier?

00:05:54.890 --> 00:05:57.100
But we just got the notice today.

00:05:57.300 --> 00:05:58.930
There's no time to waste!

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:02.350
Why's he in such a hurry?

00:06:02.690 --> 00:06:03.350
Okay!

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:05.480
Today's the big day!

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:08.230
Show me the fruits of your training!

00:06:08.230 --> 00:06:09.190
Teacher!

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:12.990
I'm the type who does well without ever training!

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:14.120
Don't say that out loud!

00:06:14.490 --> 00:06:17.330
Anyway, you better show some
backbone in the team chicken fight!

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:20.080
The fundamental strategy is to rush
in from all sides and whack 'em good!

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:23.710
So attack from their weak side, right?

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:25.750
But we only need to take their hat...

00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:27.000
Hitting people's kinda...

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:28.550
Don't sweat the little stuff.

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:31.010
That's one of those mistakes of youth.

00:06:31.010 --> 00:06:32.550
So we're just boys.

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:38.560
Sis!

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:39.560
Do your best!

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:41.260
Good luck!

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:43.940
Hey.

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:47.480
How is that anpan attached to the string?

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:51.150
It's probably attached to a clip or something.

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:54.570
So you can't take it off very easily.

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:56.320
Bring us victory!

00:06:56.530 --> 00:06:58.450
Girls must be elegant!

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:00.750
Like an eating contest could ever be elegant!

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:01.330
Ready!

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:12.090
She did it!

00:07:18.220 --> 00:07:19.930
That's Kagamin for you.

00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:27.020
That person has an incredible camera.

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:34.900
Man, he's so easy to understand.

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:36.160
Hey.

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:38.450
Aren't you in the 100 meter dash next?

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:39.660
Technically.

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:42.660
How can I learn to run fast like you?

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:45.000
It's important to visualize.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:46.250
Visualize.

00:07:48.790 --> 00:07:50.030
Ready!

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:51.670
Set!

00:07:54.010 --> 00:07:56.680
That's one ancient visualization.

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:03.430
Goal!

00:08:03.810 --> 00:08:04.770
Like that?

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:05.600
Are you serious?

00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:10.560
3 meters and 25 centimeters.

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:13.530
So they measure from where your hands reached.

00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:19.370
<i>This is it!</i>

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:23.240
That's Kagami.

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:24.830
Dived straight into the sand, huh?

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:28.710
<i>One, two, three.</i>

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:30.630
<i>One, two, three.</i>

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:34.420
<i>I've heard that timing your
steps is important for hurdles.</i>

00:08:34.420 --> 00:08:36.050
<i>Steps?</i>

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:36.970
<i>One.</i>

00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:38.010
<i>Two.</i>

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:39.220
<i>Three.</i>

00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:40.390
<i>I get it!</i>

00:08:40.390 --> 00:08:42.970
<i>One, two, three.</i>

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:44.100
Set!
<i>One, two, three.</i>

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:44.600
<i>One...</i>

00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:46.390
<i>Um...</i>

00:08:46.390 --> 00:08:47.480
<i>Three, two, three!</i>

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:49.730
<i>One, three, huh?</i>

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:51.060
Um...

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:52.730
I started with my right foot so...

00:08:55.610 --> 00:08:56.780
I don't get it!

00:08:56.900 --> 00:08:58.270
That was my left foot so...

00:08:59.570 --> 00:09:00.870
Three, three, three.

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:02.070
Three, two, three...

00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:05.540
She's knocking every single one down.

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:06.700
You could say she's got talent.

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:08.710
Geez Louise.

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:12.670
I totally sucked.

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:13.420
Man...

00:09:13.420 --> 00:09:14.210
I told you.

00:09:14.210 --> 00:09:16.920
I thought my daughter was in this.

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:18.470
A common occurrence.

00:09:19.470 --> 00:09:21.340
It's finally time for the last relay.

00:09:21.340 --> 00:09:22.220
Yuki-chan!

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:23.390
Do your best!

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:23.930
No...

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:25.260
I told you that my daughter's...

00:09:25.260 --> 00:09:25.430
I'll do my best!

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:26.770
Hold on a second!

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:28.520
I haven't even done anything yet!

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:29.600
Okay!

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:30.230
Go for it!

00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:31.190
Pedal to the metal!

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:33.560
Awesome!

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:34.900
We're in second!

00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:35.940
Not bad.

00:09:35.940 --> 00:09:37.230
Sachi, over here!

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:42.320
Okay!

00:09:45.530 --> 00:09:46.950
We've fallen to third.

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:48.790
This is what you call a race.

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:50.400
Keep at it!

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:51.040
Okay!

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:54.750
They're working pretty hard.

00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:56.300
This is getting interesting.

00:09:57.880 --> 00:10:00.590
Will Yuki-chan be okay?

00:10:09.430 --> 00:10:14.360
Okay.

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:25.240
Go, Miyuki!

00:10:32.580 --> 00:10:33.620
Yay!

00:10:33.620 --> 00:10:35.060
Yuki-chan's so cool!

00:10:35.060 --> 00:10:36.790
That's our Miyuki-san.

00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:40.010
Didn't forget to give the spectators some eye candy.

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:51.390
<i>It's Tsukasa.</i>

00:10:52.020 --> 00:10:53.140
<i>Oh, well.</i>

00:10:54.060 --> 00:11:00.150
<i>Happy Henry Likes Beer But Could Not Obtain Food.</i>

00:11:19.880 --> 00:11:20.670
Hey!

00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:22.800
Can you do something about that?

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:23.920
Sorry.

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:27.800
I chose to play the alto part
in a quartet for music class...

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:29.930
...but my fingers are getting numb.

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:33.350
Why did you choose the alto part?

00:11:33.350 --> 00:11:37.150
I-I thought the lower part might be easier.

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:41.280
Why don't you condition your
fingers on an easy song for now?

00:11:56.670 --> 00:11:58.670
You missed most of the notes.

00:11:59.420 --> 00:12:01.590
So try to match me.

00:12:01.590 --> 00:12:02.460
Ready and...

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:08.180
H-Hold on!

00:12:08.180 --> 00:12:09.930
Play by yourself.

00:12:18.980 --> 00:12:20.650
Somehow seems wrong...

00:12:20.980 --> 00:12:23.230
Try blowing a little softer.

00:12:23.610 --> 00:12:26.790
If you relax, it might go a lot better.

00:12:27.150 --> 00:12:28.360
I see.

00:12:28.360 --> 00:12:29.320
Softer...

00:12:29.320 --> 00:12:30.240
That's it.

00:12:30.780 --> 00:12:31.910
I'll give it a try.

00:13:00.690 --> 00:13:03.730
<i>Isn't she doing more breathing than playing?</i>

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:09.360
I was thinking we should
try the cafeteria occasionally...

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:10.780
...but it sure is crowded.

00:13:10.990 --> 00:13:12.530
It's pretty overwhelming.

00:13:12.530 --> 00:13:15.330
And waiting in line is annoying and exhausting.

00:13:15.330 --> 00:13:16.540
Sure sucks.

00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:19.790
Haven't you gotten used to
this kind of thing from those events?

00:13:19.790 --> 00:13:23.750
When I'm not eagerly anticipating what
awaits me at the end of the line, it sucks.

00:13:23.960 --> 00:13:26.630
True to your desires, huh?

00:13:26.630 --> 00:13:27.510
That's right.

00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:29.880
I went to a theme park once...

00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:32.550
...and thought that I had lined up for an attraction...

00:13:32.550 --> 00:13:34.720
...but the line was for the restroom.

00:13:34.720 --> 00:13:38.810
It's a fundamental rule to
check what the line is for first.

00:13:38.980 --> 00:13:40.980
And I waited two whole hours...

00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:43.730
I've also gotten in line a few times...

00:13:43.730 --> 00:13:45.980
...and when it was finally my turn...

00:13:45.980 --> 00:13:49.070
...the person before me had bought the last one.

00:13:49.070 --> 00:13:50.110
Terrible...

00:13:50.110 --> 00:13:51.610
Don't even wanna picture it.

00:13:51.740 --> 00:13:53.530
You're just unlucky.

00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:56.240
Look, everyone.

00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:57.830
What shall we have today?

00:13:58.250 --> 00:14:00.000
Well, I guess I'll go with curry.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.170
They can't screw it up...

00:14:01.170 --> 00:14:02.790
I'll go with ramen.

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:03.920
Me too.

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:06.550
I was planning on having miso ramen today.

00:14:06.550 --> 00:14:07.920
With lots of corn...

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:09.760
...and seaweed, too!

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:12.380
Kagami's probably having ramen,
pudding, and an éclair.

00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:14.950
If I have enough room to eat more.

00:14:17.890 --> 00:14:19.720
You always have more room.

00:14:20.600 --> 00:14:21.850
What about you, Yuki-chan?

00:14:21.850 --> 00:14:23.600
I'll have a sandwich.

00:14:23.600 --> 00:14:25.260
With strawberries.

00:14:25.770 --> 00:14:27.640
Sounds like something you would have.

00:14:27.900 --> 00:14:28.690
Right?

00:14:28.690 --> 00:14:29.940
By the way...

00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:33.110
Isn't a strawberry sandwich considered dessert?

00:14:33.110 --> 00:14:35.200
Would it count as lunch?

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:36.580
Th-That's true...

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:38.790
You pick some odd issues to be concerned about.

00:14:39.580 --> 00:14:42.120
What about those chocolate cornets you always have?

00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:43.790
Wouldn't sweet pastries be considered dessert?

00:14:44.330 --> 00:14:46.780
<i>Stupid Tsukasa has the gall to give me lip...</i>

00:14:47.460 --> 00:14:49.300
Anyway, moving on...

00:14:49.590 --> 00:14:51.550
Unfortunately, Miyuki-san...

00:14:51.880 --> 00:14:54.200
The line for sandwiches is over there.

00:14:55.090 --> 00:14:56.350
Typical behavior.

00:14:56.350 --> 00:14:58.600
Walking is healthy.

00:14:58.970 --> 00:14:59.470
Look.

00:14:59.470 --> 00:15:00.640
It's your turn, Kona-chan.

00:15:01.480 --> 00:15:02.520
Curry please.

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:03.600
With extra sauce.

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:04.480
Okay.

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:05.900
You're pretty shrewd.

00:15:05.900 --> 00:15:08.090
I'll take what I can get.

00:15:10.530 --> 00:15:10.820
Okay.

00:15:10.820 --> 00:15:11.990
Next person?

00:15:11.990 --> 00:15:13.490
Soy sauce ramen please.

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:14.780
With hard noodles.

00:15:14.780 --> 00:15:16.650
Okay, please wait one moment.

00:15:17.570 --> 00:15:17.990
Okay.

00:15:17.990 --> 00:15:19.720
Here's your curry.

00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:23.710
I'll go get a table.

00:15:23.710 --> 00:15:24.040
Countin' on you.

00:15:24.040 --> 00:15:25.370
Thanks!
Countin' on you.

00:15:26.210 --> 00:15:26.790
Let's see...

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:27.820
Next person?

00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:29.000
Yes.

00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:31.090
Can I please have miso ramen?

00:15:31.090 --> 00:15:32.090
Sorry.

00:15:32.090 --> 00:15:34.130
The last person ordered the last of our noodles.

00:15:34.130 --> 00:15:36.020
We're out of ramen.

00:15:37.260 --> 00:15:38.050
Say.

00:15:38.050 --> 00:15:40.310
If you're okay with soy sauce, do you want mine?

00:15:40.310 --> 00:15:42.640
I'm okay with fox udon.

00:15:42.640 --> 00:15:44.770
Thank you, Sis.

00:15:51.150 --> 00:15:52.450
Hey, Sis.

00:15:53.530 --> 00:15:57.280
You're the older sister because
you came out first, right?

00:15:57.280 --> 00:15:58.030
Yeah.

00:15:58.280 --> 00:16:00.700
I was thinking that it's a good
thing I'm the younger sister.

00:16:01.450 --> 00:16:02.290
Why?

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:08.420
Because an older sister shouldn't be asking a
younger sister for help with homework and stuff.

00:16:08.420 --> 00:16:12.800
I'm pretty sure that copying homework
has nothing to do with that.

00:16:13.010 --> 00:16:14.760
Besides, we're twins.

00:16:14.760 --> 00:16:16.680
Neither of us is really older or younger.

00:16:16.680 --> 00:16:17.590
Stop worrying...

00:16:17.590 --> 00:16:19.340
...and do your homework.

00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:24.520
<i>But if I were the older sister...</i>

00:16:24.520 --> 00:16:27.060
<i>...and all dependable and responsible...</i>

00:16:27.940 --> 00:16:29.270
Sis!

00:16:29.270 --> 00:16:30.860
Show me your homework!

00:16:30.860 --> 00:16:31.980
Again?

00:16:31.980 --> 00:16:34.440
You're so hopeless, Kagami.

00:16:35.530 --> 00:16:36.030
Hey.

00:16:36.030 --> 00:16:36.360
That was wack!

00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:37.490
You okay there?

00:16:37.490 --> 00:16:38.780
Get a grip.
That was wack!

00:16:39.030 --> 00:16:40.120
I did it!

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:40.990
Newtype...

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:42.240
...published my...

00:16:42.240 --> 00:16:43.490
...very own...

00:16:43.620 --> 00:16:45.200
...postcard!

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:47.960
In the May issue...

00:16:48.170 --> 00:16:48.370
Saitama province.

00:16:48.370 --> 00:16:48.960
The one that has Akira-chan standing on Shiraishi.

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:50.500
Konata Izumi.

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:51.460
The one that has Akira-chan standing on Shiraishi.

00:16:51.460 --> 00:16:51.790
Good for you.

00:16:51.790 --> 00:16:52.420
Look at it!

00:16:52.420 --> 00:16:53.590
Kinda amazed they published this.

00:16:55.340 --> 00:16:56.720
A-Amazing!

00:16:56.720 --> 00:16:57.760
What a surprise!

00:16:57.760 --> 00:16:59.300
This is pretty rare, yeah?

00:16:59.300 --> 00:17:00.970
Like, seriously, huh?

00:17:00.970 --> 00:17:03.930
Now I have one more thing to look forward to buying!

00:17:03.930 --> 00:17:05.430
You don't need to praise me so much!

00:17:07.940 --> 00:17:09.940
<i>1,260 yen...</i>

00:17:09.940 --> 00:17:12.940
<i>...and 567 yen, huh?</i>

00:17:13.150 --> 00:17:16.440
<i>I'll have enough points after one more book.</i>

00:17:16.650 --> 00:17:19.320
<i>Then I should just get something...</i>

00:17:19.320 --> 00:17:19.860
<i>No.</i>

00:17:19.860 --> 00:17:21.820
<i>Then I'd be falling into their trap.</i>

00:17:21.820 --> 00:17:24.120
<i>I'm not so easy to fool.</i>

00:17:24.490 --> 00:17:27.550
<i>That would be an unplanned
purchase for the sake of points.</i>

00:17:27.550 --> 00:17:29.500
<i>That's their strategy.</i>

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:34.250
<i>I'm not dumb enough to fall for that trick.</i>

00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:35.670
<i>Oh!</i>

00:17:36.550 --> 00:17:38.260
<i>I forgot that the fifth volume was out.</i>

00:17:38.260 --> 00:17:38.630
<i>Okay!</i>

00:17:38.630 --> 00:17:39.880
<i>This works!</i>

00:17:52.730 --> 00:17:54.230
<i>Oh, well.</i>

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:00.150
I can't get it loose.

00:18:00.150 --> 00:18:01.070
I'm sorry.

00:18:01.990 --> 00:18:03.070
I don't want to let go.

00:18:03.070 --> 00:18:03.200
Yes...

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:06.620
I thought that only ever happened in manga or games...

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:08.620
...but it actually happens in real life.

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:09.910
Guess so.

00:18:09.910 --> 00:18:11.210
Which means...

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:14.460
Those two definitely triggered a flag.

00:18:14.460 --> 00:18:15.540
Konata...

00:18:15.540 --> 00:18:18.550
Fantasy refers to the world of illusion.

00:18:18.550 --> 00:18:21.010
Can't tell the difference between dreams and reality?

00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:28.020
Good lucky!

00:18:28.470 --> 00:18:31.180
I come with a dreamer's heart to spread love again!

00:18:31.180 --> 00:18:34.900
I'm Lucky Channel's navigator, Akira Kogami!

00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:36.480
And I'm the assistant.

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:38.070
Minoru Shiraishi.

00:18:38.070 --> 00:18:42.070
We've already reached the
eighth episode of this program.

00:18:42.070 --> 00:18:43.570
That's true.

00:18:43.570 --> 00:18:45.570
If we don't come up with some fresh material...

00:18:45.570 --> 00:18:47.120
...we'll be accused of abusing mannerisms.

00:18:47.120 --> 00:18:47.950
What was that?

00:18:48.790 --> 00:18:50.640
<i>What am I doing?!</i>

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:51.540
No.

00:18:51.540 --> 00:18:53.080
I just wanted to try some new things...

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:53.920
You said it.

00:18:53.920 --> 00:18:54.620
I just wanted to try some new things...

00:18:54.620 --> 00:18:55.380
You know...

00:18:55.380 --> 00:18:55.880
Do it.

00:18:56.420 --> 00:18:57.210
That's right!

00:18:57.210 --> 00:18:58.840
I was walking around town the other day...

00:18:58.840 --> 00:19:00.090
...and someone came up to talk to me.

00:19:00.380 --> 00:19:01.800
Was it some salon doing a survey?

00:19:02.020 --> 00:19:04.090
Geez, Shiraishi-san.

00:19:04.090 --> 00:19:05.800
Do you actually mean that?

00:19:06.720 --> 00:19:08.760
Of course, it was a fan.

00:19:08.760 --> 00:19:10.560
This would never happen to you...

00:19:10.560 --> 00:19:11.430
Right?!

00:19:11.430 --> 00:19:13.020
I-I-I-I-It wouldn't!

00:19:16.310 --> 00:19:17.150
That's true...

00:19:17.150 --> 00:19:17.980
Right?!

00:19:17.980 --> 00:19:19.360
You're the assistant...

00:19:19.360 --> 00:19:20.190
Right?!

00:19:20.190 --> 00:19:22.280
Well, keep workin' hard.

00:19:23.490 --> 00:19:24.400
B-But...

00:19:24.400 --> 00:19:25.700
I've already received this many...

00:19:25.700 --> 00:19:26.620
A oopsie-daisy.

00:19:26.620 --> 00:19:27.320
...fan letters!

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:30.120
H-How?!

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:31.240
Hey, Itou!

00:19:31.240 --> 00:19:31.330
Haven't I gotten any?!

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:31.870
<i>Incredible.</i>

00:19:31.870 --> 00:19:33.330
<i>I feel like a real voice actor.</i>
Haven't I gotten any?!

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:35.500
So I did get some.

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:37.450
Only one?

00:19:38.170 --> 00:19:41.590
Your membership has almost expired...

00:19:41.590 --> 00:19:42.460
Hey!

00:19:42.460 --> 00:19:44.760
This is that stupid online service!

00:19:44.760 --> 00:19:46.430
Everybody who's watching!

00:19:46.430 --> 00:19:50.010
Please send me fan letters, too!

00:19:50.310 --> 00:19:52.850
Big, big, big recruitment drive!

00:19:54.180 --> 00:19:55.190
Akira-sama.

00:19:55.190 --> 00:19:56.520
Shouldn't we get to today's topic...

00:19:56.520 --> 00:19:58.060
Don't get too cocky.

00:19:58.060 --> 00:20:00.400
You're easily replaceable.

00:20:00.860 --> 00:20:02.320
I'm so sorry.

00:20:02.940 --> 00:20:03.860
Ta-da!

00:20:03.860 --> 00:20:05.740
I have an announcement to make!

00:20:05.740 --> 00:20:06.360
Wow!

00:20:06.360 --> 00:20:08.240
We'll be creating figures on this program!

00:20:08.240 --> 00:20:08.910
Akira-sama!

00:20:08.910 --> 00:20:09.450
The clipboard!

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:10.950
The clipboards upside-down!

00:20:11.620 --> 00:20:13.450
Oh, you're doing it on purpose!

00:20:13.450 --> 00:20:15.080
You're a genius, Akira-sama!

00:20:15.080 --> 00:20:16.210
Actually...

00:20:16.210 --> 00:20:17.830
...this project is...

00:20:17.830 --> 00:20:18.460
Peel.

00:20:18.460 --> 00:20:19.330
P-Peel. Peel.

00:20:19.670 --> 00:20:21.000
Peel. Peel. Peel.
Don't touch me.

00:20:21.960 --> 00:20:22.340
Huh?

00:20:22.340 --> 00:20:23.550
That's weird.

00:20:24.460 --> 00:20:27.200
This project is...

00:20:27.590 --> 00:20:29.610
Don't touch me.

00:20:30.890 --> 00:20:32.180
This is...

00:20:33.930 --> 00:20:34.390
Peel.

00:20:37.600 --> 00:20:39.530
What's wrong with this thing?!

00:20:41.020 --> 00:20:42.860
H-H-Hey, Seishi!

00:20:42.860 --> 00:20:44.150
I got it, okay!
A-Akira-sama, calm down!

00:20:44.150 --> 00:20:44.990
That's the name of your manager in real life!

00:20:44.990 --> 00:20:47.280
This is my prop!

00:20:47.280 --> 00:20:49.410
Could you have...

00:20:49.410 --> 00:20:50.070
Of course not!

00:20:50.070 --> 00:20:50.620
Okay!

00:20:50.620 --> 00:20:57.080
Then we'll decide which figure
to make based on your votes!

00:20:57.080 --> 00:21:00.920
Have fun waiting for us to
turn the character into a figure!

00:21:01.380 --> 00:21:03.840
Everyone, please vote!

00:21:03.840 --> 00:21:04.420
Okay.

00:21:04.420 --> 00:21:06.210
That's all for today.

00:21:06.210 --> 00:21:08.840
Look forward to next week's Lucky Channel!

00:21:08.840 --> 00:21:10.750
Bye-bee!

00:21:12.850 --> 00:21:16.430
A character from the actual show's
obviously gonna win the poll.

00:21:16.430 --> 00:21:17.430
What's with this?

00:21:17.430 --> 00:21:18.560
Like I have a chance in hell.

00:21:18.560 --> 00:21:20.690
No, you can't be sure yet.

00:21:21.060 --> 00:21:21.400
I see.

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:22.610
They're finally going to make a figure of me.

00:21:22.610 --> 00:21:23.480
What are you talking about?

00:21:23.480 --> 00:21:24.520
This is...

00:21:26.070 --> 00:21:27.940
That was great, Yuki-chan!

00:21:27.940 --> 00:21:29.610
Thank you for listening.

00:21:29.610 --> 00:21:31.950
I never expected this side of you.

00:21:31.950 --> 00:21:32.820
Please...

00:21:32.820 --> 00:21:34.370
It's embarrassing.

00:21:34.370 --> 00:21:35.740
Hey, Yuki-chan.

00:21:35.740 --> 00:21:37.180
Let's sing a song together.

00:21:37.660 --> 00:21:38.620
Let's do that.

00:21:39.210 --> 00:21:40.290
Sing! Sing!

00:21:40.290 --> 00:21:41.460
A duet, huh?

00:21:41.460 --> 00:21:42.790
Which song do you know?

00:21:42.790 --> 00:21:43.920
Let's see...

00:21:43.920 --> 00:21:46.210
Then I'll sing a song while we're waiting.

00:21:46.210 --> 00:21:47.630
There's never gonna be a break, huh?!

00:21:47.630 --> 00:21:50.010
You should also sing!

00:21:52.260 --> 00:21:53.300
What is this?

00:21:53.300 --> 00:21:54.760
Journey to the West.

00:21:54.760 --> 00:21:57.390
Machaaki's Son Goku was great.

00:21:57.390 --> 00:21:58.180
Huh?

00:21:58.180 --> 00:21:59.640
Wasn't it Shingo-chan?

00:21:59.640 --> 00:22:01.650
That was the third remake.

00:22:01.650 --> 00:22:05.900
This one ran from 1978 to 1980.

00:22:05.900 --> 00:22:07.900
The original series!

00:22:07.900 --> 00:22:09.660
How old are you?!

00:22:11.910 --> 00:22:13.450
This is a long intro.

00:22:13.450 --> 00:22:17.580
This was when the actors delivered the main narration.

00:22:17.580 --> 00:22:18.870
Like I would know!

00:22:20.410 --> 00:22:21.400
Here it comes!

00:22:23.540 --> 00:22:25.000
You're shouting again?!

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:50.070
Born from an egg on a mountain top.

00:22:50.070 --> 00:22:52.030
It's in English. Forget that.

00:22:52.030 --> 00:22:54.630
That's it after all this build-up?

00:22:56.950 --> 00:22:59.240
Well, next time on Lucky Star:

00:22:59.240 --> 00:23:00.700
I'm Miyuki.

00:23:00.750 --> 00:23:04.460
When describing an enormously large object...

00:23:04.670 --> 00:23:08.460
...it is described as being super-dreadnought.

00:23:08.460 --> 00:23:10.590
The word dreadnought in this expression...

00:23:10.590 --> 00:23:15.050
...was derived from a British
ship commissioned in 1906...

00:23:15.050 --> 00:23:17.970
...the HMS Dreadnought.

00:23:17.970 --> 00:23:18.760
In other words...

00:23:18.760 --> 00:23:20.310
...something super-dreadnought...

00:23:20.310 --> 00:23:23.520
...would be larger than a dreadnought-class battleship.

00:23:23.520 --> 00:23:25.810
Well, that was the original meaning...

00:23:25.810 --> 00:23:27.190
...but now...

00:23:27.190 --> 00:23:31.860
...it's being used in the former context.

00:23:31.860 --> 00:23:32.780
Next time:

00:23:32.780 --> 00:23:33.860
Just a Feeling.

00:23:34.650 --> 00:23:36.200
Look forward to next time!
